-- TYPE occurrence 2/3: a record PATTERN head (`recPatHead`).  `checkPat` routes
-- `PRec` here and NOT through its `PCon` arm, so neither ambiguity peer sees this
-- position by default — without its own guard it is silent while a signature is
-- flagged.  No signature on `sizeOf`, so `Crate` occurs exactly once.
--
-- ⚠️ `Crate` is used here because it is the TYPE spelling of the head, which is
-- what `typeAmbiguous` is keyed by.  A record head may equally be a CTOR-ONLY
-- spelling (`data T = MkT { fx : Int }` → head `MkT`); that half is #1253, drained
-- by #1319 unit 1 and pinned by the `k_recpat` / `k_reclit` cells beside this one.
--
-- ⚠️ THIS CELL ALSO PINS THAT THE TWO PEERS DO NOT DOUBLE-REPORT.  `Crate` is in
-- BOTH ambiguity sets — a record's sole variant carries the type's own name — so a
-- record head that concatenated the two verdicts would emit one collision twice and
-- this cell's single row would become two.  `ambiguousHeadErrors` returns exactly
-- one verdict; that is what keeps this golden at one row per occurrence.
import ta.{Crate}
import tb.{Crate}

sizeOf (Crate { crateSz = n }) = n
